---
import { ArrowUpRight, Check } from "@lucide/astro"
---

<section id="mental-model" class="relative w-full overflow-hidden py-24 md:pt-40 md:pb-24">
  <div class="relative mx-auto w-full max-w-295 px-4">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 md:gap-12">
      <div>
        <p
          class="mb-3 font-mono text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground"
        >
          // The Mental Model
        </p>
        <h2 class="max-w-lg text-2xl leading-tighter font-semibold text-foreground md:text-3xl">
          Track successes, errors, dependencies in one type
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-lg text-lg text-muted-foreground">
          The type signature tells you everything. The compiler catches what you miss. No more
          runtime surprises.
        </p>

        <ul class="mt-5 m-0 list-none space-y-2 p-0">
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
            <Check class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-brand" aria-hidden="true" />
            <span
              >No more <code class="text-foreground font-mono">catch (e: unknown)</code> - errors are
              fully typed</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
            <Check class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-brand" aria-hidden="true" />
            <span>Dependencies are explicit - nothing is hidden</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
            <Check class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-brand" aria-hidden="true" />
            <span>Async is structured - no more promise chains you cannot follow</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="mental-model-diagram flex items-center justify-center">
        <div class="relative w-full max-w-md">
          <div
            aria-hidden="true"
            class="pointer-events-none absolute -inset-4 rounded-2xl opacity-30 blur-xl"
            style="background: radial-gradient(ellipse at center, var(--hero-glow-a) 0%, transparent 70%);"
          >
          </div>

          <div
            class="relative w-full border border-border-strong bg-card/50 px-6 py-4 font-mono text-base text-center"
          >
            <span class="mental-model-type-line">
              <span class="text-foreground">Effect</span><span class="text-subtle-foreground"
                >&lt</span
              ><span data-part="success" class="mental-model-part text-brand">Success</span><span
                class="text-subtle-foreground"
                >,
              </span><span data-part="error" class="mental-model-part text-destructive">Error</span
              ><span class="text-subtle-foreground">, </span><span
                data-part="requirements"
                class="mental-model-part text-violet-600 dark:text-violet-400">Requirements</span
              ><span class="text-subtle-foreground">&gt;</span>
            </span>
          </div>

          <svg
            class="mt-2 h-8 w-full"
            viewBox="0 0 400 32"
            fill="none"
            preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
            <path
              d="M100 0 L100 16 L67 16 L67 32"
              stroke="var(--subtle-foreground)"
              stroke-width="1"
              stroke-opacity="0.5"></path>
            <path
              d="M200 0 L200 32"
              stroke="var(--subtle-foreground)"
              stroke-width="1"
              stroke-opacity="0.5"></path>
            <path
              d="M300 0 L300 16 L333 16 L333 32"
              stroke="var(--subtle-foreground)"
              stroke-width="1"
              stroke-opacity="0.5"></path>
          </svg>

          <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-4 text-sm">
            <div data-part="success" class="mental-model-part text-center">
              <p class="font-medium text-foreground">Success</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-muted-foreground">What it returns</p>
            </div>
            <div data-part="error" class="mental-model-part text-center">
              <p class="font-medium text-foreground">Error</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-muted-foreground">What can fail</p>
            </div>
            <div data-part="requirements" class="mental-model-part text-center">
              <p class="font-medium text-foreground">Requirements</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-muted-foreground">Dependencies needed</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-4 md:mt-8 border border-border-strong bg-card/50 p-6 font-mono text-sm">
            <div class="mental-model-code-line">
              <span class="text-foreground">Effect</span><span class="text-subtle-foreground"
                >.</span
              ><span class="text-prose-foreground">gen</span><span class="text-subtle-foreground"
                >(</span
              ><span class="text-violet-600 dark:text-violet-400">function*</span><span
                class="text-subtle-foreground">() {"{"}</span
              >
            </div>
            <div class="mental-model-code-line mt-1 pl-4">
              <span class="text-violet-600 dark:text-violet-400">const </span><span
                class="text-prose-foreground">example</span
              ><span class="text-subtle-foreground"> = </span><span
                class="text-violet-600 dark:text-violet-400"
                >yield*
              </span><span class="text-prose-foreground">someOtherEffect</span>
            </div>
            <div class="mt-1">
              <span class="text-subtle-foreground">{"})"}</span>
            </div>
            <div
              class="mt-3 border-t border-border pt-3 text-xs leading-relaxed text-subtle-foreground"
            >
              <ul class="m-0 list-none space-y-1 p-0">
                <li class="grid grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-x-2">
                  <span aria-hidden="true">-</span>
                  <span>
                    <span class="text-violet-600 dark:text-violet-400">yield*</span> gives you the
                    <span class="text-prose-foreground"> Success </span>value
                  </span>
                </li>
                <li class="grid grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-x-2">
                  <span aria-hidden="true">-</span>
                  <span>
                    <span class="text-prose-foreground">Errors</span> and
                    <span class="text-prose-foreground"> dependencies</span> are tracked in the parent
                    Effect
                  </span>
                </li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-2 text-center">
            <a
              href="https://x.com/mattpocockuk/status/1937563378123260269"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-muted-foreground no-underline transition-colors hover:text-foreground hover:no-underline"
            >
              Why Effect was designed this way
              <ArrowUpRight class="h-3.5 w-3.5" aria-hidden="true" />
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .mental-model-part {
    transition: opacity 200ms ease;
  }

  .mental-model-type-line {
    display: inline;
    white-space: normal;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }

  .mental-model-code-line {
    white-space: normal;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .mental-model-diagram:has([data-part="success"]:hover) [data-part]:not([data-part="success"]),
  .mental-model-diagram:has([data-part="error"]:hover) [data-part]:not([data-part="error"]),
  .mental-model-diagram:has([data-part="requirements"]:hover)
    [data-part]:not([data-part="requirements"]) {
    opacity: 0.45;
  }
  @supports not selector(:has(*)) {
    .mental-model-part {
      opacity: 1;
    }
  }
</style>
